{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1446210-what-sort-of-addiction-flaws-are-good-for-a-nephilim","id":1446210,"title":"What sort of addiction flaws are good for a Nephilim?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-04-27T19:08:11-07:00","id":1446210,"title":"What sort of addiction flaws are good for a Nephilim?","content":"I was thinking of the Nephilim Merit and how it requires you to take three points of Physical Flaws. I think three minor addictions might cut it, to underscore that the character is partially a being from another world who depends on more than just food, water, and air. <br /> <br /> I was thinking holy water, which he might carry with him in capsules that he take three times daily, for his first addiction. Special incense, made from a variety of plants that correspond to his angel parent, which he can take by way of an inhaler as a second. What would make a good third physical dependency/addiction that he could take as a flaw? I want them to be real but ultimately manageable. <br /> <br /> Maybe his diet requires silver or gold, on top of potassium and iron? I haven\u2019t settled on anything yet, so I am looking for ideas. They don\u2019t even have to be anything like addictions as long as they are interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","user":"Mercurial","date":". 04-28-2021, 10:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-28T00:14:52-07:00","id":1446231,"title":"","content":"Must listen to choir music.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-28T04:12:03-07:00","id":1446266,"title":"","content":"Gold, frankincence, and myrrh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-28T06:26:38-07:00","id":1446280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1446210-what-sort-of-addiction-flaws-are-good-for-a-nephilim#post1446210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was thinking holy water, which he might carry with him in capsules that he take three times daily, for his first addiction.</div> </div> </div> </div>This one while inetresting does lead to some extra questions. What is the definition of Holy Water you are using - is it water with a Faith score? Thus needing to come from a source that grants it this score, which makes it a difficult item to obtain, especially for use three times a day. Or is it water that has just had the appropriate rites said over it?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26145-babi_gog","name":"babi_gog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-28T07:33:59-07:00","id":1446287,"title":"","content":"I might recommend blessed salt rather than holy water. It's slightly more obscure and (slightly) harder to get ahold of, but not unreasonable. You can fill a few bottles of holy water at any Catholic Church without anyone raising an eyebrow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-28T09:43:50-07:00","id":1446298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>babi_gog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1446210-what-sort-of-addiction-flaws-are-good-for-a-nephilim?p=1446280#post1446280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This one while inetresting does lead to some extra questions. What is the definition of Holy Water you are using - is it water with a Faith score? Thus needing to come from a source that grants it this score, which makes it a difficult item to obtain, especially for use three times a day. Or is it water that has just had the appropriate rites said over it?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The latter, but it has to be done at a place of worship for an Abrahamic faith by a recognized member of the clergy, and it cannot be more than a month old.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-28T12:28:18-07:00","id":1446317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1446210-what-sort-of-addiction-flaws-are-good-for-a-nephilim?p=1446298#post1446298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The latter, but it has to be done at a place of worship for an Abrahamic faith by a recognized member of the clergy, and it cannot be more than a month old.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you just like the symbolism or overtones or are you thinking of specific reasons for these addictions? The two you've chosen are rich in meaning and tradition so there is a lot of opportunity to dig deep if you so choose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-28T13:46:58-07:00","id":1446324,"title":"","content":"I think he just needs a certain, mild level of Resonance applied in the correct ways. It doesn\u2019t have to be anything major, I just want his physical flaws to be cool. He is a life form from two worlds and so has complicated (but not overly cumbersome) needs.<br /> <br /> Edit: If he gets some water with actual faith points invested in it, then that should have a permanent shelf life and maybe satisfy him for a month or more.<br /> <br /> Edit: Any thoughts as to what the third flaw should be?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","user":"Mercurial","date":". 04-28-2021, 06:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-28T17:01:09-07:00","id":1446376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>babi_gog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1446210-what-sort-of-addiction-flaws-are-good-for-a-nephilim?p=1446280#post1446280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This one while inetresting does lead to some extra questions. What is the definition of Holy Water you are using - is it water with a Faith score? Thus needing to come from a source that grants it this score, which makes it a difficult item to obtain, especially for use three times a day. Or is it water that has just had the appropriate rites said over it?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It would depend on how many points the Flaw is worth. For a 3pt Addiction, definitely would need its own Faith score. If it's just a 1pt Addiction, any old priest could bless that. Heck, if the Nephilim was an ordained priest, they could do it themselves. Low level addictions are the realm of having a tobacco habit. It's more intended for flavor than anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-29T05:38:49-07:00","id":1446437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1446210-what-sort-of-addiction-flaws-are-good-for-a-nephilim?p=1446324#post1446324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think he just needs a certain, mild level of Resonance applied in the correct ways. It doesn\u2019t have to be anything major, I just want his physical flaws to be cool. He is a life form from two worlds and so has complicated (but not overly cumbersome) needs.<br /> <br /> Edit: If he gets some water with actual faith points invested in it, then that should have a permanent shelf life and maybe satisfy him for a month or more.<br /> <br /> Edit: Any thoughts as to what the third flaw should be?</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly the shelf life thing isn't much of an issue given how readily available holy water is. As a point of trivia, though, the Catholic stance on holy water is that the blessing doesn't expire unless the water does, and since they frequently add blessed salt...<br /> <br /> As for a third addiction, well, you've chosen two very bodily elements already, that is, very physical sides of human worship. Perhaps the third should speak more to your character's angelic nature, maybe something to do with saying his name or something like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-30T21:41:41-07:00","id":1446736,"title":"","content":"Hmm... I am not sure. Since he will be a Hermetic I want him to have Flaws that do not eat up his time the way some activity oriented flaws might. Bathing in water that has been mixed with blessed salts could work, but I am still looking for any suggestions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}